   209	\paragraph{Problem source.}
   210	The paramagnetic torus executes the Carnot refrigeration cycle
   211	1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 1 shown in Figure 3b in the H-versus-T plane.  T\_h and T\_c
   212	are the hot- and cold-reservoir temperatures; Q\_h is the magnitude of heat
   213	delivered to the hot reservoir and Q\_c is the magnitude absorbed from the cold
   214	reservoir.  The equation of state is T*M*V = n*K*H and the isothermal heat
   215	relation from part B may be reused.
   216	
   217	Current subquestion:
   218	A body of heat capacity C\_c is cooled from T\_0 to T while refrigerator input power P and hot-reservoir temperature T\_h remain constant. Determine the elapsed time.
   219	
   220	\paragraph{Current subquestion.}
   221	A body of heat capacity C\_c is cooled from T\_0 to T while refrigerator input power P and hot-reservoir temperature T\_h remain constant. Determine the elapsed time.
   222	
   223	\paragraph{Recorded answer/context.}
   224	t = (C\_c*T\_h/P)*[ln(T\_0/T) - (T\_0 - T)/T\_h].
